{"id":"00000001794531028633:d649ffb3bd4464539a0d3df81d0d81c1","text":"Owner direction (Nate, 2026-11-13 00:48Z, inbox i-1794530812667-81314-0): asked 'Should One's binding generator emit per-class modules so apps only bundle the iOS classes they use (option 1)?', Nate answered '1' (Yes, do option 1). Notes from p250205 (size owner), INFERRED from reading One origin/main a5008847e7: (1) wire.ts wrapHandle picks the JS wrapper from the registerSDKClass registry with superclass fallback, so if a framework barrel stops registering every class, user code that receives a class it never imported at runtime gets a plainer wrapper; keep one/ios/<Framework> registering everything and move only One's backends (22 files, ~40 symbols) to per-class imports. (2) Frameworks hold ~1000-2250 exports each, so a per-symbol module per export adds thousands of Metro modules for user code that imports a whole framework; group per class with its nested types or measure the overhead. (3) The lazy-first-call fix in this task's body only cuts bytes if the bundler splits the dynamic import; plain Metro still bundles the modules. Lane lead decides the design."}
